## Input resolution - TWO ORTHOGONAL AXES

Parse `$ARGUMENTS`. The first token matching a scope keyword sets `{SCOPE}` (default `session`). The token `hard`
anywhere - or the same intent in prose - sets `{DEPTH}` = `HARD`. Everything else is free-form `{FOCUS}`.

**`{SCOPE}` selects WHICH CHANGES drive the sync:**

| `{SCOPE}` | Change-fact source |
|-----------|--------------------|
| `session` (DEFAULT) | What THIS conversation did: new modules, renames, removals, env vars, migrations, commands, behaviour changes. The COORDINATOR writes the change-fact list from its own context - no gather agent for it |
| `branch` | `git diff $(git merge-base HEAD "$MAIN")..HEAD`, where `$MAIN` is DERIVED (`git symbolic-ref --short refs/remotes/origin/HEAD 2>/dev/null` -> `origin/<name>`, else the bare `{DEFAULT_BRANCH}`; both are valid revisions). NEVER hardcode `main` |
| `commit <sha>` / `commit <a>..<b>` | `git show <sha>` / `git diff <a>..<b>` |
| `recent[:N]` | `git diff HEAD~N..HEAD`, default N=10 |
| `all` | NO diff - EVERY checkable fact in every memory file is re-verified against current code |

**`{DEPTH}` selects HOW HARD:**

| `{DEPTH}` | Behaviour |
|-----------|-----------|
| `NORMAL` (DEFAULT) | fact sync + dedup + compression |
| `HARD` | NORMAL plus the TWO aggressive passes in `references/hard-sync.md`: rules `paths:` PRECISION audit and OBVIOUS-KNOWLEDGE PURGE. Triggered by the token `hard` or semantically ("почисти жёстко", "too much context", "aggressive", "cut it down") |

> **The axes are independent.** `all hard` re-verifies everything AND purges; `session` (no token) is the cheap
> default. Depth never changes which files are swept; scope never changes how hard they are cut.

**`{FOCUS}` is EMPHASIS ONLY - a hard rule.** Free-form focus text re-ORDERS effort inside the sweep; it NEVER
narrows it, never drops a batch, never skips a file. "only rules" means *rules first and hardest*, not *rules
alone*. A run that touched only one layer because the user named that layer is a DEFECTIVE run.

> **Standing emphasis:** {FOCUS_EMPHASIS}
> Facts stay ahead of dedup, and dedup ahead of compression, whatever the emphasis. The order may be SHARPENED,
> never inverted.

**ANNOUNCE - print this PLAN block before any work:**

```
[memory-sync] PLAN
Scope:   {SCOPE} - {matched token | "default (no scope token)"}
Depth:   {DEPTH} - {matched signal | "default NORMAL"}
Focus:   {FOCUS interpretation | "standing emphasis"} (emphasis only - full surface still swept)
Batches: {batch: N files, ...}   (re-enumerated this run)
Fan-out: {N} gather (Explore) + {M} sync (one per non-empty batch) + {K} verify (Explore, one per EDITED batch) agents intended
```

**PHASE STATUS - print ONE chat line at every phase boundary:**
`[memory-sync] Phase {N} {name} - started|done: {key numbers}` (facts collected, files inventoried, batches
spawned, files edited, lines delta, verdicts ok).

