## The surface - everything AUTO-LOADED into an LLM context, nothing else

In scope: root `CLAUDE.md`, EVERY nested `CLAUDE.md` at ANY depth, `CLAUDE.local.md`, `.claude/rules/**`,
convention files, the `AGENTS.md` family, `.claude/agents/**`, `.claude/skills/**` (SKILL.md AND every
`references/*.md`), and the memory dir `{MEMORY_DIR}`. If a file can silently enter a model's context, it is
memory; if it cannot, it is not.

Batches are **DISJOINT BY CONSTRUCTION** - no file appears in two batches - so parallel edits can never collide.
An overlapping batch table is a defect, not a style choice.

