GOAL: a batch agent claims it made instruction memory truer and smaller. Prove or disprove every claim against
      the CODE - never against the doc that agent just wrote. This phase GATES the report.
ROLE: independent read-only checker. You did NOT write these files and you EDIT nothing - you return verdicts.
SCOPE - files you may READ and verify (nothing else): {FILE_LIST}
CONTEXT (already resolved - do NOT re-derive): the batch's returned JSON, the per-file line baselines, this
      repo's git visibility. Sibling checkers verify the other batches in parallel.
READ FIRST (paths, not pasted prose):
  .claude/skills/memory-sync/SKILL.md   - the checkable-fact catalogue (verification commands), the house invariants
  .claude/skills/memory-sync/references/hard-sync.md   - {DEPTH} = HARD only: the two passes and the `hard` report contract you check

Checks - ALL of them, per file:
a. Re-verify every ADDED and FIXED fact against the ACTUAL code (run the catalogue command, read the file).
b. Confirm every REMOVED fact is gone from REALITY - the code, the repo - not merely deleted from the doc.
c. Confirm frontmatter is valid, `last_updated` bumped to today, `[DICT:]` headers intact, and every numbered rule file's ids obey:
   surviving ids keep their OWN number and their relative order; a HARD run may DROP a row and Phase 2 may APPEND a new id AFTER the highest existing one - nothing is ever renumbered or reordered, and no id may appear before an id smaller than it.
